<StaticPage
	title="About PawsomeFlock"
	description="Learn about PawsomeFlock, our mission, and the person behind the cat, dog and bird guides you read here."
	icon="🐾"
>
	<p>
		PawsomeFlock started with a simple idea: pet parenting advice online is scattered, contradictory,
		and often written by people who don't actually own the pets they're writing about. We wanted one
		place where cat, dog, and bird owners could find clear, practical, no-nonsense guidance — the kind
		you'd get from a friend who's been through it, not a content farm.
	</p>
	<p>
		Every guide on this site is organized by topic — feeding, health, training, gear, and everyday care
		— so you can find the specific answer you need instead of wading through generic "top 10" lists.
	</p>

	<h2>Who's behind PawsomeFlock</h2>
	<div class="author-card">
		<img src="/derrick_radley.png" alt="Derrick Radley" class="author-photo" />
		<div>
			<p class="author-name">Derrick Radley</p>
			<p class="author-role">Founder &amp; Editor, PawsomeFlock</p>
		</div>
	</div>
	<p>
		Hi, I'm <strong>Derrick Radley</strong>, the person writing and editing the guides on PawsomeFlock.
		My interest in pet care started with a rescue cat named Milo, who came into my life as a nervous,
		underweight stray and quickly taught me that good pet parenting is about much more than buying the
	right food or choosing the right toy. It is about paying attention, learning your pet's habits, and
		being willing to change when something isn't working.
	</p>
	<p>
		Over the years, dogs and birds became part of my everyday life too. I've made plenty of beginner
		mistakes along the way — from overcomplicating feeding routines to buying products that looked great
		online but were completely impractical at home. Those experiences are a big reason I started
		PawsomeFlock. I wanted to document the useful lessons, the mistakes, and the simple solutions I
		wish someone had explained to me when I was starting out.
	</p>
	<p>
		Today, I focus on turning pet-care questions into practical, easy-to-follow guides. I spend time
		checking reliable sources, comparing advice, and looking at the everyday details that can make a
		real difference to a cat, dog, or bird and the person caring for them. I'm still learning too, and
		I'm comfortable saying when something is outside my experience or belongs in the hands of a
		qualified veterinary professional.
	</p>
	<div class="note-box">
		<span class="note-icon">🩺</span>
		<span>
			I'm not a veterinarian, and nothing on this site is a substitute for professional veterinary care —
			you can read more about that in our <a href="/disclosure/">Disclosure &amp; Disclaimers</a> page.
			What I can offer is research, first-hand experience, and an honest attempt to cut through the noise.
		</span>
	</div>

